M3.1 — exact/regex/path surfaces (commit 727814a)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Before: RepositoryIndex::exact()/regex() had NO production caller.
- TaskIndex::query_exact/query_regex: bounded direct surfaces (path-
  ordered hits with line+snippet; invalid regex = typed IndexError).
- context.query mode=fused|exact|regex|path; all direct modes refresh
  from the change journal first and record retrieval evidence.
- E2E (daemon, turns c5/c6): exact + regex against content created
  mid-run by change.apply.
- MUTATION CHECK: regex surface disabled — FIRST ATTEMPT PASSED (the
  assertion matched the mode label, not real hits); hardened to require
  the body-line snippet ("snippet":"true", a line appearing nowhere else
  in the conversation) — the mutation then FAILED the E2E. Both the
  false-pass and the fix are recorded deliberately.

M3.7 — planner-routed auto mode
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Before: modbit_context::planner (dynamic query planning) was logic-only
with zero production callers.
- TaskIndexWriter::query_auto: REAL index signals (bounded exact probe,
  symbol-defined check, term count, structural/engineering phrasing) →
  planner::plan → MINIMUM sufficient level: L0 exact / L1 hybrid
  (fused) / L2 structural (symbol surface) / L3 engineering (fused ×2,
  later + import-impact). The plan (level, rationale, signals) rides
  every auto response. auto is the tool default. (docs/18: LLM rerank
  optional, NOT required for P0 — rerank.rs stays unwired.)
- E2E (REAL daemon, 9-10 turns): multi-term → hybrid; "definition of X"
  → structural; bare defined identifier → EXACT (no over-escalation —
  the REQ ledger EV-0001 core); architectural phrasing → engineering.
- Honest iteration: the first c7 expectation assumed a bare identifier
  routes to structural; the planner correctly chose the cheaper L0
  exact. The TEST was fixed, not the planner.
- MUTATION CHECK: planner bypassed (all forced hybrid) → the
  structural/engineering/exact routing assertions FAILED (dump shows
  every turn "rationale":"mutated"). REVERTED; post-revert green.

M3.6 — import/dependency evidence graph + impact mode (commit 685047b)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Before: context_graph.rs offered a line-shape parser with no production
caller; no real import edges existed anywhere.
- crates/retrieval/dependencies.rs (new): tree-sitter extraction of use/
  import edges — Rust (crate:: → src/ trees and root layouts, super::/
  self:: climbing, externals dropped), TS/TSX/JS (relative specifiers,
  candidate extensions + index files), Python (dotted + relative with
  __init__.py packages) — resolved deterministically against the
  indexed corpus; self-edges dropped; only corpus targets kept.
- TaskIndex: deps index maintained by build_at AND apply_delta
  (re-extract changed, drop deleted, prune edges into evicted targets);
  impact(path, depth) = transitive dependents with hop counts (bounded
  BFS, deterministic ordering).
- Production surface: context.query mode=impact (dependents + hops +
  test-file flag); the M3.7 L3-engineering route now carries
  impact_of_top_hit (note updated honestly: diagnostics/runtime
  evidence still pending — M3.4 and the M3.6 remainder).
- Tests: 5 dependency unit tests (per-language resolution, prune,
  impact BFS) + task_index integration (edges survive build and
  incremental deltas).
- E2E (REAL daemon): the fixture gains a real import (caller.rs →
  helpers.rs via `use crate::helpers;`); turn c10 impact query proves
  the EDITED file's dependent appears at hop 1 in the durable
  conversation; turn c8's L3 answer carries impact_of_top_hit.
- MUTATION CHECK: edge extraction disabled (env-gated) → the E2E FAILED
  at "the import dependent appears at hop 1" (impact returned empty
  dependents). REVERTED; post-revert green.

